<title>USA: Potlatch wins $95 mln jury award.</title>
<headline>Potlatch wins $95 mln jury award.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Potlatch Corp and an Idaho jury has awarded the company $95 million for damages from defects and deficiencies of a pulp washer system that was installed in the company's Lewiston, Idaho, pulp mill.</p>
<p>The washers were supplied by Beloit Corp, the defendant. The trial was held in Idaho District Court in Lewiston, Idaho, Potlatch said in a statement issued late Tuesday.</p>
<p>Potlatch filed its complaint against Beloit in December 1995. The trial began in April 1997.</p>
<p>Beloit has said it plans to appeal the verdict.</p>
<p>Potlatch is a forest products company.</p>
</text>
